  "kanji": "美",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 美\ntitle: beauty\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 9\nradical: 羊\nradicalNumber: 123\nonyomi: [ビ, ミ]\nkunyomi: [うつく.しい]\ndistractors: [着, 大, 春]\n---\n\n# 美 — beauty\n\n**Strokes:** 9 · **Key (radical):** 羊 (no. 123) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n美 concerns beauty: something pleasing to look at, hear, or appreciate.\n[美しい](../words/美しい.md) うつくしい is the adjective \"beautiful.\"\n美術 びじゅつ brings the same character into the vocabulary of art.\n\nThe indexing radical 羊 forms the horned upper portion above 大; it is not a separate full-height 羊 beside 大.\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** picture that horned top and the broad 大 below as a frame around an impressive artwork.\nThis is a modern visual aid, not an origin story.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| うつく.しい | kun | [美しい](../words/美しい.md) うつくしい — beautiful |\n| ビ | on | 美術 びじゅつ — art; fine arts |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [美しい](../words/美しい.md) うつくしい — beautiful\n- 美術 びじゅつ — art; fine arts\n\n## Notes\n\nThe table leaves ミ to the metadata. 美しい attaches directly to a noun:\n美しい声 (うつくしいこえ), \"a beautiful voice.\"\n[着](着.md) has a similar upper outline, but its lower part is not 大.\n[大](大.md) and [春](春.md) provide simpler lower-part and stacked-shape comparisons.\n",
